   "source": [
    "# 2. Data: collection and cleaning\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2.1 Sources\n",
    "\n",
    "| Source | Content | Collection |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **Global Integrated Power Tracker**, Global Energy Monitor, September 2026 | One row per power unit (183,404 rows): technology, capacity, status, start year, owners, location | Excel file mirrored, unchanged, on a public URL of our SSP Cloud storage (CC BY 4.0), downloaded by the code |\n",
    "| **World Bank API** | Income group, GDP per capita and Regulatory Quality (Worldwide Governance Indicators) for each country | Automated queries of the public API, with pagination |\n",
    "| **ISO country codes** (datasets/country-codes, GitHub) | Country names and ISO codes | CSV read from a public URL; used to join the two sources above |\n",
    "| **Sponsor dictionary** (`data/sponsors.csv`) | 30 companies, their name patterns and home country | Built by hand from public information |\n",
    "\n",
    "Global Energy Monitor (GEM) is a non-profit that tracks energy infrastructure worldwide\n",
    "from public sources: regulators, company reports, local press. The tracker covers power\n",
    "plants above size thresholds that vary by technology and sometimes by country (for\n",
    "instance, coal units from 30 MW; in this release, the smallest solar and wind units\n",
    "listed are 1 MW). Its key feature for us is the **status** of each\n",
    "unit: from *announced* to *operating*, including *cancelled* and *shelved* projects.\n",
    "Abandoned projects are rarely kept in other databases, which only list plants that exist."
   ]
  },
