  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a10840c6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Missing values are concentrated in three columns:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Parent companies** (`parents`) are only reported for coal, gas and some other\n",
    "  thermal plants, where GEM links each owner to its ultimate parent.\n",
    "- **Owners** (`owners`) are missing for half of the units, but these are mostly small\n",
    "  solar projects in Europe and Asia: owners are known for 89% of the capacity worldwide,\n",
    "  and for over 90% of the capacity in the Middle East.\n",
    "- **Start year** is missing for most projects that are not yet operating, which is\n",
    "  expected: they have no start date yet. It is known for 90% of operating units.\n",
    "\n",
    "These gaps shape our method: we cannot follow projects over time (no announcement date),\n",
    "and our analysis of owners leaves out many small projects."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4a1adeba",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.3 Cleaning the unit table\n",
    "\n",
    "The function `clean.build_units` applies five steps, each in its own function:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Select and rename** the useful columns (snake_case names).\n",
    "2. **Group the ten statuses into four stages**: *pipeline* (announced and pre-construction),\n",
    "   *construction*, *operating* and *abandoned* (cancelled and shelved, including inferred\n",
    "   statuses). Retired and mothballed units go into *other*. The mapping is defined in\n",
    "   `config.STATUS_TO_STAGE`; the function raises an error if GEM introduces a new status.\n",
    "3. **Add readable labels**: technology names, and a regional grouping (GCC, rest of the\n",
    "   Middle East, rest of the world).\n",
    "4. **Add ISO country codes**, needed to join the World Bank data.\n",
    "5. **Flag the units that reached an outcome** (defined in 2.4).\n",
    "\n",
    "We also drop two units with a capacity of zero and check that unit identifiers are unique."
   ]
  },
