   "source": [
    "### 2.7 Enrichment: country data from the World Bank API\n",
    "\n",
    "We query the World Bank API (`src/worldbank.py`) for three country characteristics:\n",
    "\n",
    "- the **income group** (low, lower-middle, upper-middle, high income);\n",
    "- **GDP per capita** in current US dollars;\n",
    "- **Regulatory Quality**, one of the Worldwide Governance Indicators. It measures\n",
    "  perceptions of the government's ability to design and implement policies that allow\n",
    "  and promote private sector development, on a scale from about -2.5 to +2.5.\n",
    "\n",
    "The API returns paginated JSON; the code loops over pages, keeps the most recent\n",
    "non-missing value for each country, and drops regional aggregates (\"World\", \"Arab World\").\n",
    "Indicator codes of the governance indicators changed in 2024, so the code tries the new\n",
    "code first and falls back on the old one. A snapshot of the result is saved in\n",
    "`data/worldbank_snapshot.csv`, so that the notebook still runs if the API is unavailable."
   ]
  },
