  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1d3a07ab",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The contrast between the three panels is the starting point of our question:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Operating**: the region runs on gas and oil (417 GW), far ahead of solar (34 GW).\n",
    "- **Under construction**: gas still dominates (83 GW, including Iran and Iraq), ahead of\n",
    "  solar (27 GW) and wind (16 GW).\n",
    "- **Pipeline**: the picture reverses. Solar (139 GW) and wind (80 GW) dominate the announced\n",
    "  projects, ahead of gas (77 GW).\n",
    "\n",
    "The region announces an energy transition, but what it builds today is mostly gas.\n",
    "Whether the renewable pipeline will be built is exactly the question of development risk."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e98a74fa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
