   "source": [
    "gcc_abandoned = (\n",
    "    units.loc[(units[\"area\"] == \"GCC\") & units[\"abandoned\"]]\n",
    "    .groupby([\"project\", \"country\", \"technology\", \"status\"], as_index=False)[\"capacity_mw\"].sum()\n",
    "    .sort_values(\"capacity_mw\", ascending=False)\n",
    "    .head(10)\n",
    ")\n",
    "display(gcc_abandoned.style.format({\"capacity_mw\": \"{:,.0f}\"}).hide(axis=\"index\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "gcc_by_technology = indicators.abandonment_rate(units.loc[units[\"area\"] == \"GCC\"], \"technology\")\n",
    "display(gcc_by_technology[[\"technology\", \"abandoned_gw\", \"built_gw\", \"abandonment_rate\"]]\n",
    "        .style.format({\"abandoned_gw\": \"{:,.1f}\", \"built_gw\": \"{:,.1f}\",\n",
    "                       \"abandonment_rate\": \"{:.0%}\"}).hide(axis=\"index\"))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7029cbf4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Abandonment in the Gulf has three identifiable causes:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Policy changes**: all coal projects (6.7 GW) were cancelled, including the Ras\n",
    "  al-Khaimah and Ajman plants and the last units of Dubai's Hassyan plant, which was\n",
    "  converted to gas (its gas units appear as operating in the data).\n",
    "- **Stalled public-private partnerships in Kuwait**: several large gas plants procured by the\n",
    "  Kuwait Authority for Partnership Projects (Al-Khairan, Doha East, Shuaiba South) were\n",
    "  shelved. This explains Kuwait's 46%.\n",
    "- **Projects tied to green hydrogen**: very large solar farms planned to power hydrogen or\n",
    "  ammonia plants in Abu Dhabi and Oman, or announced without a buyer (North Kuwait Solar,\n",
    "  Duqm) were shelved.\n",
    "\n",
    "By contrast, gas projects, which feed the region's growing demand and are bought by\n",
    "state utilities, have an abandonment rate of only 6%.\n",
    "\n",
    "The map below shows each project of the Middle East that reached an outcome, with circles\n",
    "proportional to its capacity."
   ]
  },
